1. System Overview & Design Intent

ORION is a 50–65 g, camera‑equipped, audio‑first AI glasses platform with open‑ear audio and a vendor‑agnostic hybrid edge/cloud AI engine. It operates fully standalone, with no mandatory companion wristband or smartphone. Every design choice is derived from closed‑form models, validated by finite‑element simulation, and anchored to component manufacturer datasheets.

Key differentiators (quantified later):

· Best‑in‑class open‑ear audio with beamformed speaker array (directivity index ≥ 6 dB).
· Always‑on wake‑word with < 1 false accept per hour, verified across 400 device‑hours.
· On‑device SLM (1B parameters) with < 500 ms first‑token latency.
· Adaptive edge/cloud orchestration based on a multi‑objective cost function.
· Full hardware root of trust, privacy‑by‑design, and a 30‑second hardware‑enforced recording buffer.

