2.2 Dynamic Power State Machine

Finite state machine with states defined by vector $(A, C, N, B)$: Audio activity, Camera on, Network active, Battery level. Power $P(s)$ per state. Transitions governed by user intent and autonomy policy.

Cost‑function for state transitions:

J(s \rightarrow s') = \alpha \cdot \Delta P + \beta \cdot L_{\text{trans}} + \gamma \cdot \mathbb{I}_{\text{thermal violation}}

where $L_{\text{trans}}$ is perceived latency, $\alpha,\beta,\gamma$ tunable weights. Implementation as a lookup table on the DSP.

