7. Battery & Energy Storage Model

7.1 Detailed Battery Model

Chemistry: Li‑polymer, 220 mAh rated, 3.85 V nominal, 4.35 V charge. Cell datasheet parameters:

· Internal resistance: 150 mΩ (new), rising to 350 mΩ at end‑of‑life.
· Discharge curve: empirical fit $V(SOC) = 3.85 + 0.35\cdot \ln(SOC/(1-SOC))$, $SOC\in[0.05,0.95]$.
· Usable capacity: $C_{\text{useful}} = C_{\text{rated}} \cdot \eta_{\text{temp}} \cdot \eta_{\text{aging}}$, where $\eta_{\text{temp}} = 1 - 0.005(T-25)$ for $T>25\ \mathrm{°C}$.

Runtime integration: Run‑time is solved by integrating current consumption over the mixed‑use profile, using the cell model.
Confirmed 3.3 h at 25 °C (coincides with simple averaging). At 40 °C ambient, capacity de‑rated by 7.5 % → 3.0 h.

7.2 Battery Aging & Cycle Life

Capacity fade model:

C(N) = C_0 \cdot \left(1 - a\cdot N^{b}\right)

· $a = 0.002$, $b = 0.6$ (fitted from cell cycle data).
· After 300 cycles: $C(300) = C_0 (1 - 0.002\cdot 300^{0.6}) = C_0 (1 - 0.002\cdot 30.6) = 0.939\,C_0$ → ~6 % fade.
· After 500 cycles: ~91 % capacity remaining.
  End‑of‑life defined as 80 % → > 1000 cycles. Manufacturer‑guaranteed 500 cycles to 80 %.

Temperature acceleration: Arrhenius factor $\exp(0.08\cdot (T-25))$, doubles fade at 55 °C (not expected in normal use).

