13. Reliability Engineering & Weibull Analysis

13.1 MTBF Calculation

Using MIL‑HDBK‑217F and vendor FIT rates for key components:

· SoC: 200 FITs
· Battery cell: 50 FITs
· MEMS mics: 10 FITs each (×8 = 80)
· Total system: ~500 FITs → MTBF = 2 000 000 hours (228 years).

13.2 Early Life Failures (Weibull)

Shape parameter $\beta = 1.2$ (mixed failure modes).
Require > 95 % survival at 1 year (8760 h). Given MTBF, survival probability $R(t) = e^{-(t/\eta)^\beta}$, with $\eta = \text{MTBF} / \Gamma(1+1/\beta) \approx 2.2e6 \text{ hours}$, $R(8760) \approx 0.9999$ — far exceeds target.

