Appendix F: Battery Model & Ageing Data

F.1 Electrical Model (Second‑Order RC)

· OCV vs SOC: 3.85 + 0.35·ln(SOC/(1−SOC)), 0.05 ≤ SOC ≤ 0.95
· Series resistance $R_0$ = 0.15 Ω (new), 0.35 Ω (EOL)
· RC pairs: $R_1$=0.05 Ω, $C_1$=2000 F; $R_2$=0.02 Ω, $C_2$=5000 F (transient response)
· Fitted from manufacturer EIS data, used in Simulink digital twin.

F.2 Capacity Fade Equation

· Cycle fade: $C(N)=C_0 (1 - a N^b)$ with $a=0.002$, $b=0.6$ (25 °C, 1 C charge/discharge)
· Calendar fade: additive 2 % per year at 25 °C, 4 % at 35 °C
· Combined end‑of‑life criterion: 80 % of initial capacity.

F.3 Temperature Impact

· Discharge capacity: $C(T) = C_{25} \times [1 - 0.005(T-25)]$ for $T > 25\ \mathrm{°C}$
· At −10 °C: capacity ~85 %, internal resistance doubled; system throttles peak power.

